518
01:10:41,300 --> 01:10:48,140
This is the behavior of static analysis on Python when changing the domain model in ORM-based projects.

519
01:10:48,140 --> 01:11:02,140
The fact is that I have been working on the same project for several years, and one of the problems with the growth of the code base that I have discovered is that it is quite difficult to predict

520
01:11:02,140 --> 01:11:07,380
how much refactoring will be needed if we change, for example,

521
01:11:07,380 --> 01:11:11,700
from one type to another in order to some field.

522
01:11:11,700 --> 01:11:21,140
We have faced this problem, and people in the literature have faced this problem.

523
01:11:21,140 --> 01:11:25,460
It's good that we have a type, we changed it,

524
01:11:25,460 --> 01:11:30,740
if we use a static type, the static analyzer immediately showed it to us,

525
01:11:30,740 --> 01:11:44,280
But we have these fields like lines, we have these fields like bare SQL, we have these fields somewhere in JSON, and there are a lot of such things.

526
01:11:44,280 --> 01:11:49,660
And sometimes static analysis does not always show all the places that need to be shown.

527
01:11:49,660 --> 01:11:58,980
And the operation that I called for changing the domain model from one type to another is called abstract entity.

528
01:11:58,980 --> 01:12:10,980
There is an article on this account, it was published last year, and it shows that this is a big problem even today in software development.

529
01:12:10,980 --> 01:12:19,980
As I said, the team uses MyPy and Pyrite to find out what has broken.

530
01:12:19,980 --> 01:12:27,980
There are problems that interfere with full analysis.

531
01:12:27,980 --> 01:12:40,980
Speaking of literature, such problems have already been considered, but most of them are on Java, C Sharp and other projects.

532
01:12:40,980 --> 01:12:54,980
Also, given that we are now living in the age of artificial intelligence, some articles tried to find out how much LLM helps in the search for such problems.

533
01:12:54,980 --> 01:12:59,980
But the results are not very satisfactory. Precision 28, Recall 36.

534
01:12:59,980 --> 01:13:07,980
And very few works that analyze how Python feels about this.

535
01:13:07,980 --> 01:13:13,980
Moreover, we are talking about static analysis, these are tools such as MyPy.

536
01:13:13,980 --> 01:13:23,980
And only 15% of defects are found in MyPy.

537
01:13:23,980 --> 01:13:29,980
Moreover, the standard problem is that different tools show different amounts of errors.

538
01:13:29,980 --> 01:13:38,480
What gaps do I want to cover with my diploma?

539
01:13:38,480 --> 01:13:46,480
The first is that there is no research that shows how changes in the domain model on Python projects

540
01:13:46,480 --> 01:13:51,480
affect how much refactor will need to be brought.

541
01:13:51,480 --> 01:14:02,240
The second point is that there is no research on how projects based on Python and using ORM are subject to such a problem.

542
01:14:02,240 --> 01:14:08,480
